+\section{Preregistered falsification gates}
 \label{sec:programme}
 
-The positive content established here is a consistency architecture:
-
-\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
-  \item The apparent conflict between compact and filament energy normalizations is exactly resolved: their density ratio is the volume ratio $1/(2\alpha)=68.518$ (\cref{prop:volume}).  Two ontologies, one arithmetic.
-  \item The model's contact with data is exactly one dimensionless number; the three available comparisons are algebraically identical (\cref{prop:residual}), with common residual $-855.13$~ppm.
-  \item The closure determines the medium density, not the coupling: $\alpha$ cancels identically (\cref{eq:master-identity}).  On the quantized branch the density takes the parameter-free value $\rho_C=(2/\pi)m_e/\lC^3=1.007\times10^{7}\ \mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}$ (\cref{eq:rhoC}).
-  \item The full spread of candidate densities decomposes into two exact factors --- a volume ratio and a circulation ratio --- leaving the circulation deficit $\Gamma_{\rm eff}/\Gamma_C=\alpha^2/4$ (\cref{eq:deficit}) as the single unexplained dynamical quantity.
-\end{enumerate}
-
-This architecture is falsifiable at three separated points, each attacking a different assumption:
-
-\emph{(i) The density.}  Any independent determination of the medium density --- from a microscopic model of the medium, from a cosmological or laboratory bound on a universal inertial background, or from internal consistency of a broader framework --- must reproduce $\rho_C$ on the quantized branch (or $\rho_B$ together with a derivation of the deficit on the subluminal branch).  A mismatch falsifies the corresponding branch outright.
-
-\emph{(ii) The geometry.}  The predictor \cref{eq:alphageom} inherits the geometric provenance of the ideal-trefoil ropelength.  Improved ropelength bounds, or a demonstration that the dynamically selected conformation differs from the ideal knot (as it does for Hopf solitons \cite{Sutcliffe2007}), shift or invalidate the single residual in a fully determined way (\cref{prop:residual}).
-
-\emph{(iii) The equipartition gate.}  The comparison $D_{\rm geom}$ versus $\re$ is the hypothesis that hydrodynamic and electrostatic self-energy estimates coincide at the same scale.  A finite-core calculation of the filament energy with a declared core model and outer cutoff (\cref{sec:lognorm}) replaces the convention by a computed coefficient; if the computed coefficient moves the predicted diameter outside the shrinking uncertainty band of the comparison, the gate closes negatively.
-
-Throughout, the classical electron radius appears in exactly one role: as the observational comparison value $r_e^{\rm obs}=\alpha_{\rm obs}\lC$.  It is never an input.
